  "caption": "Quinn started a job on the shop floor, and by the end of each shift the soles were burning and tingling, even worse at night.\n\nOne possible reason: a nerve runs through a narrow tunnel behind the inner ankle bone, and swelling, a flattening arch or an old sprain can crowd it. Your lower back can cause foot symptoms too, so the whole chain is worth checking.\n\nThings that often help: roomy, supportive shoes without tight straps, settling swelling, gentle nerve glides with calf and foot strengthening, and easing off in flare-ups before building back. Progress is usually gradual.\n\nAny new numbness, weakness or burning foot pain is worth getting assessed. If you have diabetes, talk to your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
